6d2d69cf041761ed,2026-11-16T13:51:31+00:00,meeting,upcoming,El Dorado County,Legistar,El Dorado County,,Board of Supervisors,2026-11-17,Attachment: A - Strategic Plan Fall 2026 Update,https://eldorado.legistar1.com/eldorado/attachments/7cf29729-dfdd-4feb-9662-335c7994e79f.pdf,https://eldorado.legistar1.com/eldorado/attachments/7cf29729-dfdd-4feb-9662-335c7994e79f.pdf#page=6,6,false,0,housing; affordable housing; accessory dwelling unit; ADU; stormwater,25,Long Range; Science and Data,agenda,Agenda item,Agenda item,"Safe and Healthy COMMUNITIES The County is committed to creating communities where residents are safe, healthy, and supported through effective emergency response systems, coordinated public safety…",6,true,"...communities where residents are safe, healthy, and supported through effective emergency response systems, coordinated public safety partnerships, expanded housing and service opportunities, and integrated County programs designed to improve individual and community well-being. -6- 26-1798 A 6 of 28",6,false,"[{""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Safe and Healthy COMMUNITIES The County is committed to creating communities where residents are safe, healthy, and supported through effective emergency response systems, coordinated public safety…"", ""pages"": [6], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""PRIORITY: DEVELOP A CONTINUUM OF SUPPORT AND HOUSING OPPORTUNITIES FOR UNHOUSED INDIVIDUALS Action Item: Develop a comprehensive plan for affordable housing opportunities. Lead Departments: Planning…"", ""pages"": [7], ""count"": 13, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Public INFRASTRUCTURE The County is committed to maintaining, improving, and strategically investing in the infrastructure systems and public assets that support residents and County services.…"", ""pages"": [12], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""NEW! PRIORITY: STORMWATER COMPLIANCE AND INFRASTRUCTURE MANAGEMENT New! Action Item: Develop framework for enhanced interdepartmental coordination and commit to proactively strengthen program…"", ""pages"": [13], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""New! Action Item: Develop framework for enhanced interdepartmental coordination and commit to proactively strengthen program elements to implement and comply with the new 2027 National Pollutant…"", ""pages"": [13], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""PRIORITY (CONTINUED): DRIVE INNOVATION AND EFFICIENCY THROUGH THE USE OF TECHNOLOGY New ! Action Item: Utilize Power BI and Power Automate to improve data analytics, streamline workﬂows, and automate…"", ""pages"": [24], ""count"": 2, ""in_title"": false}]","[{""term"": ""housing"", ""page"": 6, ""text"": ""...communities where residents are safe, healthy, and supported through effective emergency response systems, coordinated public safety partnerships, expanded housing and service opportunities, and integrated County programs designed to improve individual and community well-being. -6- 26-1798 A 6 of 28""}, {""term"": ""housing"", ""page"": 7, ""text"": ""Safe and Healthy COMMUNITIES PRIORITY: DEVELOP A CONTINUUM OF SUPPORT AND HOUSING OPPORTUNITIES FOR UNHOUSED INDIVIDUALS Action Item: Develop a comprehensive plan for affordable housing opportunities. Lead Departments: Planning and Buildin...""}, {""term"": ""housing"", ""page"": 7, ""text"": ""...and conducted three of four workshops focused on strategies informed by the community data. These efforts will guide strategic planning related to affordable housing, transportation, and mobility needs across the County. The Affordable Housing Task Force (AHTF) continues to meet regularly and is working toward establishin...""}, {""term"": ""affordable housing"", ""page"": 7, ""text"": ""...Healthy COMMUNITIES PRIORITY: DEVELOP A CONTINUUM OF SUPPORT AND HOUSING OPPORTUNITIES FOR UNHOUSED INDIVIDUALS Action Item: Develop a comprehensive plan for affordable housing opportunities. Lead Departments: Planning and Building, Health and Human Services Agency Status: The El Dorado Community Foundation has completed 13 outreach...""}, {""term"": ""affordable housing"", ""page"": 7, ""text"": ""...responses, and conducted three of four workshops focused on strategies informed by the community data. These efforts will guide strategic planning related to affordable housing, transportation, and mobility needs across the County. The Affordable Housing Task Force (AHTF) continues to meet regularly and is working toward establishin...""}, {""term"": ""affordable housing"", ""page"": 7, ""text"": ""...ansportation, and mobility needs across the County. The Affordable Housing Task Force (AHTF) continues to meet regularly and is working toward establishing an affordable housing ordinance and developing additional strategies to promote affordable housing, as directed by the Board in Fall 2025. Next steps include completing a Nexus fe...""}, {""term"": ""accessory dwelling unit"", ""page"": 24, ""text"": ""...n. The department has enhanced transparency and customer access through online resources, including instructional videos, permit application guidance, and an Accessory Dwelling Unit ( ADU) Plans Gallery. Operational improvements include the development of internal process maps, updated Planning Division applications, state streamlining p...""}, {""term"": ""ADU"", ""page"": 24, ""text"": ""...anced transparency and customer access through online resources, including instructional videos, permit application guidance, and an Accessory Dwelling Unit ( ADU) Plans Gallery. Operational improvements include the development of internal process maps, updated Planning Division applications, state streamlining procedu...""}, {""term"": ""stormwater"", ""page"": 12, ""text"": ""...ng in the infrastructure systems and public assets that support residents and County services. Priorities include expanding broadband connectivity, enhancing stormwater compliance and infrastructure management, improving transportation planning and communication, advancing capital improvement planning, and optimizing the use...""}, {""term"": ""stormwater"", ""page"": 13, ""text"": ""...-way acquisition activities are underway. Continue to explore potential partnership opportunities for long-term connectivity goals. NEW! PRIORITY: STORMWATER COMPLIANCE AND INFRASTRUCTURE MANAGEMENT New! Action Item: Develop framework for enhanced interdepartmental coordination and commit to proactively strengt...""}, {""term"": ""stormwater"", ""page"": 13, ""text"": ""...proactively strengthen program elements to implement and comply with the new 2027 National Pollutant Discharge Elimination System (NPDES) General Permit for Stormwater Discharges from Small Municipal Separate Storm Sewer Systems (MS4s) on the West Slope. Lead Departments: Planning and Building, Transportation, Facilities, E...""}]"
