7f65ea87e0830a47,2026-11-16T13:51:31+00:00,meeting,upcoming,Washoe County,Legistar,Washoe County,,Board of County Commissioners,2026-11-17,Attachment: BCC 11-17-26 - Attachment C - NH Mtg Transcript and Public-Survey Comments,https://washoe-nv.legistar1.com/washoe-nv/attachments/c9fa27b2-c5e1-4d06-a238-0d8d5fd45673.pdf,https://washoe-nv.legistar1.com/washoe-nv/attachments/c9fa27b2-c5e1-4d06-a238-0d8d5fd45673.pdf#page=9,9,false,0,housing; affordable housing; sidewalk; transit; parking,39,Long Range; Transportation,agenda,Agenda item,Agenda item,In Portland Oregon I observed two effective means to control RV parking/living - 1) the neighbor association purchased metal oblong tanks and filled them with dirt and planted flowers. They were…,32,true,"...e street? Recording Secretary Brandon Roman: And are not moved for a year at a time? Can they be cited? Recording Secretary Brandon Roman: The trailer is not housing a person, and it's also not registered. Chad Giesinger, Planning Manager: Anything that's not registered is considered a junk vehicle, and if it's in public...",9,false,"[{""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""In Portland Oregon I observed two effective means to control RV parking/living - 1) the neighbor association purchased metal oblong tanks and filled them with dirt and planted flowers. They were…"", ""pages"": [32], ""count"": 3, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""1) the neighbor association purchased metal oblong tanks and filled them with dirt and planted flowers. They were spaced so 1 car could parallel park between them. The size for parking eliminated…"", ""pages"": [32], ""count"": 2, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""2) the city created a parking restriction - NO RV Parking allowed with signs posted on the street. The neighborhood has regained its appearance as a neighborhood and no longer an RV parking/living…"", ""pages"": [32], ""count"": 5, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""P. Bersch Strongly agree We live in a neighborhood that requires us to pay for residential parking. It is very seldomly enforced and we currently have an occupied RV parked across the street blocking…"", ""pages"": [33], ""count"": 2, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Does this mean property owners no longer need to maintain sidewalks from weeds? My husband has a mobility scooter and is unable to negotiate sidewalks that are overgrown with weeds, and worse…"", ""pages"": [39], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""My husband has a mobility scooter and is unable to negotiate sidewalks that are overgrown with weeds, and worse overgrown with goat heads that will flatten his tires. Is the reference to weeds…"", ""pages"": [39], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Chad Giesinger, Planning Manager: Had some additional language in there about being able to see things over the -foot screen, which is, if something's behind a -foot screen, it's basically supposed…"", ""pages"": [2], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": false}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Chad Giesinger, Planning Manager: Right? And that's not actually what it even said. It just said it wasn't lawfully screened. But anyways, it's being taken out. Recording Secretary Brandon Roman: So,…"", ""pages"": [9], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": false}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Chad Giesinger, Planning Manager: So, so… He's never… lmcnutt: I've never been what once? Chad Giesinger, Planning Manager: That's never been invoked once in a violation case. lmcnutt: So… Chad…"", ""pages"": [18], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": false}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Disagree Do not adopt the full code as written. Allow provisions that warrant it to go through community vetting & city-level consideration. A short delay for public input costs little; adopting…"", ""pages"": [30], ""count"": 7, ""in_title"": false}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Strongly agree Please eliminate junk cars, campers, trailers. They destroy the aesthetic view of what we were trying to be proud of.. Over the past few years I keep noticing more and more ! Strongly…"", ""pages"": [31], ""count"": 3, ""in_title"": false}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Strongly disagree You guys are just adding more stupid rules that are going to put people in jail, take their property away and fine the crap out of them in an economy where everything is already…"", ""pages"": [33], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": false}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Hi, My concern is regarding extreme noise and toxic semi truck idling throughout the day and night at Smart n Final (Reno Public Market). They allow semi trucks to just idle for hours on the Casazza…"", ""pages"": [34], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": false}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""You have not previously corresponded with this sender. Report Suspicious ‌ From: Jennifer Knowles To: Giesinger, Chad Subject: Code Enforcement [Amendment] Request Date: Wednesday, August 5, 2026…"", ""pages"": [40], ""count"": 6, ""in_title"": false}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""You have not previously corresponded with this sender. Report Suspicious ‌ From: Jay Schuler To: Giesinger, Chad Subject: New codes Date: Wednesday, August 5, 2026 5:03:37 PM Hello Chad, I just read…"", ""pages"": [43], ""count"": 2, ""in_title"": false}]","[{""term"": ""housing"", ""page"": 9, ""text"": ""...e street? Recording Secretary Brandon Roman: And are not moved for a year at a time? Can they be cited? Recording Secretary Brandon Roman: The trailer is not housing a person, and it's also not registered. Chad Giesinger, Planning Manager: Anything that's not registered is considered a junk vehicle, and if it's in public...""}, {""term"": ""housing"", ""page"": 30, ""text"": ""...is is a real issue in our region, and neighbors currently have limited recourse. I strongly oppose criminalizing people for living in RVs or vehicles amid our housing crisis. Since 2020, housing costs have surged, with home prices near $600,000 and many renters cost-burdened. Homelessness remains significant locally. Making...""}, {""term"": ""housing"", ""page"": 30, ""text"": "".... Homelessness remains significant locally. Making it a misdemeanor to sleep in a vehicle does not solve the problem—it punishes people for lacking affordable housing. Until the County expands attainable housing, enforcement-based approaches risk further destabilizing vulnerable residents rather than supporting stability....""}, {""term"": ""affordable housing"", ""page"": 30, ""text"": ""...st-burdened. Homelessness remains significant locally. Making it a misdemeanor to sleep in a vehicle does not solve the problem—it punishes people for lacking affordable housing. Until the County expands attainable housing, enforcement-based approaches risk further destabilizing vulnerable residents rather than supporting stability....""}, {""term"": ""affordable housing"", ""page"": 43, ""text"": ""...us all drink sewage. If you don’t have water, power or sewer faculties maybe the right choice is to leave what we have and save it for generations to come! Affordable housing will never happen. The only reason housing is not affordable is because we started inviting California to move here and we built built built. Raising price...""}, {""term"": ""sidewalk"", ""page"": 33, ""text"": ""...another state that is adversely affected by RV's, either abandoned or occupied, parked along entire city blocks with trash, furniture and debris blocking the sidewalk to the point where my tenants became uncomfortable accessing their leased space, I am a strong advocate of having codes and enforcement to address this type o...""}, {""term"": ""sidewalk"", ""page"": 33, ""text"": ""...orhood that requires us to pay for residential parking. It is very seldomly enforced and we currently have an occupied RV parked across the street blocking the sidewalk and also running an extension cord to the house next to it. It is not only bright and illegal. But dangerous. Agree If you could start early on the constant mu...""}, {""term"": ""sidewalk"", ""page"": 39, ""text"": "".... I have a question on the proposed changes, #4 of 50.308 where the reference to weeds is deleted. Does this mean property owners no longer need to maintain sidewalks from weeds? My husband has a mobility scooter and is unable to negotiate sidewalks that are overgrown with weeds, and worse overgrown with goat heads that w...""}, {""term"": ""transit"", ""page"": 32, ""text"": ""...occasionally. This is commercial use of a residential lot. Strongly agree Prater Way is right outside my home. It is so load by traffic (all kinds of vehicles transit this avenue); adding McCarran Ave. That Is on the other corner. The continuo traffic makes it hard to even fall sleep at night, especially on weekends. I wond...""}, {""term"": ""parking"", ""page"": 2, ""text"": ""...ations, you know, in their neighborhood, in the city. Chad Giesinger, Planning Manager: And these amendments will not apply to the city limits, or to street parking. The sheriff or the Reno PD handles stuff that happens in the street. So I just wanted to make that clear. This is only going to apply to the unincorporated a...""}, {""term"": ""parking"", ""page"": 18, ""text"": ""...unty jurisdiction, so it'd be the city codes, but the second issue is that the street right -of-way itself is in the jurisdiction of the sheriff's office, so parking for more than hours is a sheriff's office enforcement. Attachment C Page 18""}, {""term"": ""parking"", ""page"": 30, ""text"": ""...hey want and throw their trash everywhere too. They should have something near the homeless shelters where people can park and live instead of shopping center parking lots or random parking on the street. Strongly agree Strongly agree I think better control of junk and RV living is a great idea. It is an eye sore to have jun...""}]"
