505a45567b57f2a9,2026-11-16T13:51:31+00:00,meeting,upcoming,Douglas County,Granicus,Douglas County,,Board of County Commissioners,2026-11-19,Agenda packet,https://d3n9y02raazwpg.cloudfront.net/douglascountynv/23c45c5f-c4db-11f0-a7da-005056a89546-4b50c5b5-ef67-4e80-82ac-7b28f0e57fa1-1794614201.pdf,https://d3n9y02raazwpg.cloudfront.net/douglascountynv/23c45c5f-c4db-11f0-a7da-005056a89546-4b50c5b5-ef67-4e80-82ac-7b28f0e57fa1-1794614201.pdf#page=22,22,false,16,housing; workforce housing; affordable housing; sidewalk; transit; parking; vehicle miles traveled; shoreline; pier; lake clarity; stormwater; water quality,114,Long Range; Transportation; Permitting; Science and Data,agenda,Agenda item,Agenda item; Attachment,Vice Chairman Tolbert speaks: So I had the pleasure of attending a recent TRPA meeting where they presented the data that they were receiving about the clarity of the recent study. So I was surprised…,22,true,...eah. Vice Chairman Tolbert speaks: Can I? Ms. Walker speaks: Please do. Vice Chairman Tolbert speaks: So I had the pleasure of attending a recent TRPA meeting where they presented the data that they were receiving about the clarity of the recent study. So I was surprised because I don't think a lot of people...,22,false,"[{""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Vice Chairman Tolbert speaks: So I had the pleasure of attending a recent TRPA meeting where they presented the data that they were receiving about the clarity of the recent study. So I was surprised…"", ""pages"": [22], ""count"": 2, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""them when needed and coordinating with the Tahoe Regional Planning Agency on private parcel B MP certificates and updates. We have about 215 credits right now, so I feel fairly confident if we can…"", ""pages"": [24], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Tom Dallaire, Community Development Director, speaks: Yeah. It's April 15th through October 15th when the construction season is in effect. So April 15th, or I'm sorry, October 15th is when it closes…"", ""pages"": [27], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Ms. Walker speaks: Okay. I'm going to kind of skip through some of these slides because I feel like Jason covered them pretty well. But we do have plans that kind of direct our activities over time…"", ""pages"": [23], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": false}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""It's really hard to separate where stormwater runoff goes and whose runoff it is coming from. If it's coming from County maintained roads then that's considered County runoff; however, NDOT maintains…"", ""pages"": [23], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": false}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Ms. Walker speaks: Okay, so there are some challenges for us to implement the TMDL. There's not as many as there used to be, but there are 11 general improvement districts in Lake Tahoe just within…"", ""pages"": [25], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": false}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""if they're not, we have to do internal maintenance with our existing S tormwater staff. So that has to be proven every year. You have to do the inspections on the roads four times a year ; three…"", ""pages"": [26], ""count"": 2, ""in_title"": false}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Mr. Dallaire speaks: I'd just like to add the Recorder's Office is who has the file type, not the Assessor's. Yeah. No, it's the Recorder's Office. And we worked with Shawnyne on this and she has…"", ""pages"": [52], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": false}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Mr. Kirkland speaks: All right. So basically, we have about four total recommendations. There are a couple options. So the first recommendation is basically administrative updates. So one of the…"", ""pages"": [52], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": false}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""The other thing we found with some of these other programs is you can track the TDRs, but it's really creating a system where both the seller and the buyer have easy access to information. So a lot…"", ""pages"": [53], ""count"": 2, ""in_title"": false}, {""type"": ""Attachment"", ""title"": ""MULLER PARKWAY PHASE 5 – ADDITIONAL DESIGN SERVICES"", ""pages"": [384], ""count"": 3, ""in_title"": false}]","[{""term"": ""TRPA"", ""page"": 22, ""text"": ""...eah. Vice Chairman Tolbert speaks: Can I? Ms. Walker speaks: Please do. Vice Chairman Tolbert speaks: So I had the pleasure of attending a recent TRPA meeting where they presented the data that they were receiving about the clarity of the recent study. So I was surprised because I don't think a lot of people...""}, {""term"": ""TRPA"", ""page"": 22, ""text"": ""...t of other potential , the shrimp invasive species. So I guess what my question is how is ND EP participating or supporting that research with UC Davis, and TRPA, and the other members of the organization to research these factors? Because it could be that the lake herself is fighting back on her own and that some of t...""}, {""term"": ""TRPA"", ""page"": 23, ""text"": ""...hments that give us credit and one of them is through road operations. We do have some private parcel BMP registrations and we have to work closely with the Tahoe Regional Planning Agency to make sure that those certificates are kept current and updated periodically. And then we also have several water quality improvement projects, and those ar...""}, {""term"": ""TRPA"", ""page"": 23, ""text"": ""...d need to occur. The S tateline stormwater area is the casino corridor , t hey have a shared stormwater treatment facility. And we were able to work with the Tahoe Regional Planning Agency to get their BMP certificates instated because they didn't actually have them for a long time. As you can imagine, it's quite an urban area, so it does produ...""}, {""term"": ""TRPA"", ""page"": 24, ""text"": ""DOUGLAS COUNTY BOARD OF COMMISSIONERS MEETING OF OCTOBER 15, 2026 October 15, 2026 them when needed and coordinating with the Tahoe Regional Planning Agency on private parcel B MP certificates and updates. We have about 215 credits right now, so I feel fairly confident if we can continue at the level that we have...""}, {""term"": ""housing"", ""page"": 10, ""text"": ""...t at all what is part of Item 12.4 and hence is an Open Meeting violation, as should be obvious, details matter. The idea of providing attainable or workforce housing for our young families, teachers, firemen, sheriff's deputies, for instance, is a worthy goal. That, however, is not what this proposal will achieve, as curr...""}, {""term"": ""housing"", ""page"": 10, ""text"": ""...ers, firemen, sheriff's deputies, for instance, is a worthy goal. That, however, is not what this proposal will achieve, as currently constructed. Affordable housing has a very specific decision, especially when you invoke HUD, a federal agency; you are asking for trouble with that. You know who might easily qualify for th...""}, {""term"": ""housing"", ""page"": 10, ""text"": ""...ppens at 30 years, does the owner at the time get a huge windfall profit? That would encourage developers to hold on to them . Perhaps it should be affordable housing in perpetuity with the price going up with the CPI or four percent increase, whichever is higher, or something like that. Rather than rewarding people who ha...""}, {""term"": ""workforce housing"", ""page"": 10, ""text"": ""...hat is not at all what is part of Item 12.4 and hence is an Open Meeting violation, as should be obvious, details matter. The idea of providing attainable or workforce housing for our young families, teachers, firemen, sheriff's deputies, for instance, is a worthy goal. That, however, is not what this proposal will achieve, as curr...""}, {""term"": ""workforce housing"", ""page"": 42, ""text"": ""...hen you see so many vacancies , this seemed like an avenue to explore to see if the Board would be interested in trying to address our affordable housing and workforce housing concerns. I will say this is not, this is not special to Douglas County, this is not isolated in Douglas County. Affordable and workforce housing is a nationw...""}, {""term"": ""workforce housing"", ""page"": 43, ""text"": ""...ays to try to do this. That's why when AB 241 came forward, we were like, great, here's an opportunity maybe we can address the Master Plan and affordable and workforce housing. But then the T owns, respectfully, they wanted to stick with the P lans of P rosperity and that commercial component and that was understood. So then when V...""}, {""term"": ""affordable housing"", ""page"": 10, ""text"": ""...lies, teachers, firemen, sheriff's deputies, for instance, is a worthy goal. That, however, is not what this proposal will achieve, as currently constructed. Affordable housing has a very specific decision, especially when you invoke HUD, a federal agency; you are asking for trouble with that. You know who might easily qualify for th...""}, {""term"": ""affordable housing"", ""page"": 10, ""text"": ""...ms. What happens at 30 years, does the owner at the time get a huge windfall profit? That would encourage developers to hold on to them . Perhaps it should be affordable housing in perpetuity with the price going up with the CPI or four percent increase, whichever is higher, or something like that. Rather than rewarding people who ha...""}, {""term"": ""affordable housing"", ""page"": 42, ""text"": ""...sentation only. Introduction of Ordinance 2026- 1673, a Zoning Text Amendment amending Douglas County Code, Title 20, by revising section 20.664.125 to add an affordable housing exemption to the commercial floor area requirement applicable to mu lti-family housing that requires a mixed -use component. The proposed exemption does not a...""}, {""term"": ""sidewalk"", ""page"": 139, ""text"": ""...the hours specified on the permit and/or on the approved traffic control plan. All traffic control devices shall be completely removed from the roadway and sidewalk at the end of the permitted activity period. 18. PERMITTEE shall only use legalized interstate exits as turnarounds. PERMITTEE shall not use emergency veh...""}, {""term"": ""transit"", ""page"": 313, ""text"": ""...greement: (a) Race, Color, Creed, National Origin, Sex, Age -In accordance with Title VII of the Civil Rights Act, as amended, 42 U.S.C. § 2000e, and Federal transit laws at 49 U.S.C. § 5332, the Contractor agrees to comply with all applicable equal employment opportunity requirements of U.S. Department of Labor (U.S. DOL...""}, {""term"": ""parking"", ""page"": 4, ""text"": ""...ction. Discussion to approve a $66,503.95 payment from Douglas County to the Douglas County School District from profits collected during the Warrior Way Paid Parking Program season of May 1, 2026, through October 1, 2026 pursuant to an Interlocal Agreement previously entered into between Douglas County and the Douglas Count...""}, {""term"": ""parking"", ""page"": 72, ""text"": ""...lays a key role in supporting the Airport. The Facilities crew, the Roads crew out there, ensuring that there is a safe walking path to the community from the parking lot or excuse me, to the event from the parking lot, so many people showing up to support this event. Oh, and I forgot to call out for under Community Servic...""}, {""term"": ""parking"", ""page"": 140, ""text"": ""...ree of debris at all times. Removal of trash and debris will be the responsibility of the PERMITTEE. 27. PERMITTEE shall not use the NDOT right-of-way for parking or staging. All activities shall be accomplished outside of the NDOT right-of-way. EMERGENCY 28. During business hours, emergency work on permitted facili...""}, {""term"": ""vehicle miles traveled"", ""page"": 26, ""text"": ""...ut we fund the Lake Link with the South Shore Transportation Management Association. And that was originally required when the event center went in to reduce vehicle miles traveled. And all of that is related to reducing the 26""}, {""term"": ""vehicle miles traveled"", ""page"": 27, ""text"": ""...it's too indirect, but could that have any credit possibilities as well because that does create ride share. And the whole purpose of having that is to reduce vehicle miles traveled, which is to improve clarity and health of the lake. And I suppose that I'm a proponent of that because of the goal to protect the lake. But if our residents...""}, {""term"": ""shoreline"", ""page"": 270, ""text"": ""...r w/7 Way Plug + GCWR 34,000 lbs. + On Star + Cross over ignition switch for batteries + Soft Touch Driver and Passenger Seats ADVANCED POWER SYSTEM + 50amp Shoreline Connector + (2) Victron Heavy Duty Lithium Battery (300Ah) + 200w Victron Solar Charging System with Controller + Victron High Capacity Inverter/Charger + 1...""}, {""term"": ""shoreline"", ""page"": 276, ""text"": ""...r w/7 Way Plug + GCWR 34,000 lbs. + On Star + Cross over ignition switch for batteries + Soft Touch Driver and Passenger Seats ADVANCED POWER SYSTEM + 50amp Shoreline Connector + (2) Victron Heavy Duty Lithium Battery (300Ah) + 200w Victron Solar Charging System with Controller + Victron High Capacity Inverter/Charger + 1...""}, {""term"": ""shoreline"", ""page"": 284, ""text"": ""...rakes + Exhaust Brake + Power Driver and Passenger Seats + 20,000lbs Hitch + GCWR 45,999lbs + 10” touch screen w/ Phone Mirroring ADVANCED POWER SYSTEM + 50amp Shoreline Connector + (2) Victron Heavy Duty Lithium Battery (300Ah) + 200w Victron Solar Charging System with Controller + Victron High Capacity Inverter/Charger + 1...""}, {""term"": ""pier"", ""page"": 23, ""text"": ""...n. But it ended up being able to separate the stormwater runoff from the creek itself and so the credits were achieved that way. It's right next to the Sushi Pier area at the Lake there right at Stateline. And so it's a great project to check out. We also have the Oliver Park 